{
  "headline": "Yemen military holds mass funeral for 75 recruits killed in Houthi missile strike",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Yemen's military held a mass funeral on Wednesday for 75 new recruits killed during a Houthi missile strike in south-central Shabwa province. According to reporting by Africanews, the strike occurred on October 19, 2026, at the al-Alam camp while the recruits, aged between 18 and 20, were lining up in formation for a training session. The governor of Shabwa stated the recruits were being trained to provide security in the province rather than for combat operations. In addition to the fatalities, 200 others were wounded in the attack. The funeral ceremony was held in a soccer field at the site of the strike and was attended by senior government and military officials as troops and security forces carried the coffins of the deceased. Following the ceremony, the governor of Shabwa pledged to increase efforts to defend the province and vowed to pursue those responsible for the strike to hold them accountable."
    }
  ]
}

