  "headline": "Oshawa voter turnout was 18.4 per cent in 2022 ahead of 2026 municipal election",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "In the 2022 municipal election in Oshawa, Canada, 18.4 per cent of eligible residents cast a ballot. This turnout was lower than the average for the Durham Region during the same election, which was just under 24 per cent. The upcoming municipal election is scheduled for October 19, 2026, and will feature nine candidates seeking to replace outgoing Mayor Dan Carter. For the first time this year, Oshawa residents will have the option to vote online. To participate, voters must be on the voters' list. Unregistered residents can visit the voter assistance centre at Oshawa City Hall, located at 50 Centre Street S., to be added to the list. The centre is open from 10 a.m. to 6 p.m. daily until October 16, 2026."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "headline": "US embassy accuses Canada of election interference ahead of midterms",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "In a fact sheet released on October 21, 2026, the United States embassy accused Canadian politicians of attempting to influence the upcoming November 3 midterm elections. According to Al Jazeera, the US embassy alleged that the Canadian government has been dismissive of these concerns, claiming that ministers and premiers have described plans to influence American politics in public appearances and official documents. The allegations follow a trade war between the two nations that began at the start of President Donald Trump’s second term in 2025, characterized by US tariffs and reciprocal Canadian import taxes. The US embassy identified public statements regarding these tariffs as attempts to sway the midterm election, citing Canadian tariffs, political meetings, and anti-Trump advertisements as evidence of interference."
    },
    {
      "text": "The US embassy singled out Canadian Industry Minister Melanie Joly in the fact sheet, pointing to comments she made in August regarding the response to US tariffs. Joly stated at the time, “We’re also targeting products that will target states in the US. And so we’re being wise and strategic to put political pressure.” The embassy also cited Joly’s September meetings with Democratic officials in Boston and Chicago. When asked by a reporter about potential tariff outcomes if Democrats won the midterms, Joly responded, “That’s exactly why I’m meeting so many governors and potential presidential candidates.” Joly has rejected the suggestion that her actions constitute interference, stating that Canada would never meddle in US elections."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "headline": "MobileMoney Fintech LTD signs partnership to expand digital finance for MSMEs in Ghana",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "MobileMoney Fintech LTD has signed a strategic partnership with the United Nations Capital Development Fund and the United Nations Conference on Trade and Development to expand digital financial services for Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) in Ghana. The agreement was signed in Accra by Shaibu Haruna, Chief Executive Officer of MobileMoney Fintech LTD, and Allen Anie, Head of Experimentation and Chief Technical Adviser at UNDP, who initialled for the UN system. The signing was witnessed by officials from the Ministry of Trade, Agribusiness and Industry and senior management from MobileMoney Fintech LTD. Under the Joint SDG Fund programme, the partnership aims to leverage digital ecosystems to increase MSME productivity and advance financial inclusion. Shaibu Haruna stated that the programme focuses on underserved groups, specifically women and youth-led businesses, and intends to address financial health pillars including savings, micro-loans, and group loans."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "headline": "Journalist Sohrab Hossain laid to rest in Patuakhali, Bangladesh",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Md Sohrab Hossain, a correspondent for The Daily Star in Patuakhali for over 22 years and vice-president of the Patuakhali Press Club, was laid to rest on the morning of October 21, 2026, at his family graveyard in Auliapur, Patuakhali. His namaz-e-janaza was held at 10:00am at the Auliapur Sabina Akter High School grounds, attended by local residents, colleagues, fellow journalists, and relatives. During the service, his sons, Atikur Rahman and Sufian Molla, spoke. Representatives from various social, political, and professional organizations, including The Daily Star’s Content Editor Md Al-Amin and Patuakhali Press Club President Zakir Hossain, also paid their respects. Following the ceremony, Hossain was buried next to the grave of his elder brother, Maulana Wahab Molla. According to The Daily Star, Hossain joined the publication on January 1, 2004."
    },
    {
      "text": "Hossain died at Patuakhali Medical College Hospital on October 20, 2026, at the age of 55. A hospital death certificate listed cardiac arrest as the cause of death. Family members stated that on the morning of October 21, 2026, Hossain was riding a motorbike from his village home in Auliapur toward his residence at Banani Mor. At approximately 8:30am, he reportedly felt pain and stopped near the Molla bus stand before collapsing on the road. Local residents and family members transported him to the hospital, where he later died."
    }
  ]
}
